WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.890
Monday, school.

2
00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:04.230
Wednesday, a friend's house.

3
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.370
Saturday, the corner shop.

4
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:11.170
By Sunday, the map shows a dot for
almost everywhere you went this week.

5
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.550
Now the twist.

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.250
Nobody followed you.

7
00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:17.250
Every dot came from the
free game on your phone.

8
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.290
So who said a game could
know where you were all week?

9
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:24.610
In this mission, you'll see why your
location counts as personal data,

10
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:28.890
and why that data is valuable for
targeting adverts or selling on.

11
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:33.370
You'll find out what privacy means: your
right to control who sees information

12
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.430
about you.

13
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.070
And you'll ask what a free
app really gets in return.

14
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:41.280
Your mission: work out who
agreed to that tracking.
